            <div xml:id="d521">

                <pb facs="0570" n="466" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg466"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.01/67: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Culbertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-07-18T16:00:00-05:00">July 18, 1932—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:44 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>136. All my colleagues have acknowledged the note received from the Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs requesting recognition. I think it would be desirable merely
                    from the standpoint of courtesy for me to send in an informal acknowledgment
                    stating that I have transmitted the Minister’s note. Please instruct whether or
                    not I should take this step.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
